That's like how, how much you can resist getting pinned, you know, which goes down over time.

00:30:41.840 --> 00:30:46.000
You can, you can read it as you like tell how much longer it's taking you over how many

00:30:46.000 --> 00:30:52.760
more hits. But it's, and I get that like it breaks quote unquote immersion to have that like on screen.

00:30:52.860 --> 00:30:54.640
Cause if you're watching wrestling, you can't see that.

00:30:54.740 --> 00:30:56.620
But like, I don't know.

00:30:56.760 --> 00:31:00.900
I, I, I wish you could see all that, those values because this is supposed to be simulating

00:31:00.900 --> 00:31:08.200
being the wrestler and they are aware of how they're feeling and we can't do that visually.

00:31:08.200 --> 00:31:10.080
So like show us their health bars, you know?

00:31:10.360 --> 00:31:14.120
It's like, I don't, not that it's a huge complaint, but that that's just something that's

00:31:14.120 --> 00:31:18.100
stuck out. Well, now that you say that, I kind of wish that most games would also have like an emotional

00:31:18.100 --> 00:31:19.200
wellbeing meter.

00:31:21.480 --> 00:31:27.520
Yeah. Right. Did you guys feel like there was ever much reason to punch?

00:31:27.780 --> 00:31:30.060
Cause the punch is just a shorter range kick.

00:31:30.240 --> 00:31:34.960
Yeah. And more so than most games with a punch and a kick, I just felt like I'll just kick the

00:31:34.960 --> 00:31:37.780
whole time. I'm not going to get in that close and let him kick me on the way.

00:31:38.020 --> 00:31:43.560
I felt like at whatever angle you were coming at them with or getting approached by,

00:31:44.120 --> 00:31:47.000
uh, the, the kick or the punch could be more effective.

00:31:47.000 --> 00:31:52.060
Like if he's more above you than a punch would work, it doesn't really work if you're thinking

00:31:52.060 --> 00:31:58.500
about this as a 3d environment, but that, that's sort of the vibe I got, but I could not tell

00:31:58.500 --> 00:32:00.540
you if that was the correct way to go about it.

00:32:21.820 --> 00:32:25.160
Also there was a, there's like a tag team match that you can do, right?

00:32:25.400 --> 00:32:26.760
Did anybody do those tag team matches?

00:32:26.760 --> 00:32:28.800
Joe? Uh, I did.

00:32:28.960 --> 00:32:33.980
Yes. Um, so first I played a regular one-on-one match with a buddy.

00:32:34.080 --> 00:32:39.820
Then we did the tag team matches and I'm not exactly sure what triggers like your, maybe

00:32:39.820 --> 00:32:40.740
you have to be weak.

00:32:40.940 --> 00:32:44.960
What triggers your like partner to try to tag you in.

00:32:44.960 --> 00:32:52.700
But, uh, like honestly it was like a ways into the match and suddenly like one of us, I think

00:32:52.700 --> 00:32:59.480
I got hit and like this like silhouette guy shows up like on the, uh, on the other side

00:32:59.480 --> 00:33:02.880
of the rope. And it's just, it was just more like alarming for a second.

00:33:02.960 --> 00:33:04.380
I'm like, what the heck was that? Like what was that?

00:33:04.480 --> 00:33:08.580
It turns out it's like my partner, but he like appears and disappears very quickly because

00:33:08.580 --> 00:33:12.420
like, I think it, I think it's like when I walk over a certain point that triggers him

00:33:12.420 --> 00:33:15.720
to appear at certain, like after a certain amount of time, I don't know.

00:33:16.100 --> 00:33:18.600
It's like all of a sudden we had basically forgotten it was a tag team.

00:33:18.840 --> 00:33:24.480
Then he showed up, but I did tag out and it did, um, prove useful for me because I ended

00:33:24.480 --> 00:33:28.760
up winning when I was greatly losing because I tagged out and then I was able to pin him

00:33:28.760 --> 00:33:31.160
before he was able to tag out into his fresh person.

00:33:31.160 --> 00:33:35.040
So pretty, you know, nice, a nice addition, I suppose.

00:33:35.360 --> 00:33:40.600
Joe, for the tag team matches, um, and they can be played just by yourself too, for the

00:33:40.600 --> 00:33:43.340
record, you don't need a friend, uh, to do the tag team match.

00:33:44.020 --> 00:33:50.700
Um, your tag team partner will come only if you, uh, go to your team's corner and use the,

00:33:50.700 --> 00:33:53.780
uh, a button. Did you, did you go to the correct corner?

00:33:54.380 --> 00:33:59.800
Uh, so maybe his tag team partner was available too, cause I, we, we saw them appearing in both

00:33:59.800 --> 00:34:03.180
corners, but not until very late into the match.

00:34:03.320 --> 00:34:08.520
So I'm assuming there still must be like a, a threshold for your health before or time

00:34:08.520 --> 00:34:09.620
or something before they started appearing.

00:34:09.820 --> 00:34:12.440
Yeah. Maybe it's like in and out of those corners before that.

00:34:12.560 --> 00:34:17.880
Right. Maybe it's like a system where like your, your partner needs to sense you're in danger so

00:34:17.880 --> 00:34:22.520
that you can tag them in rather than just constantly tagging in and out because it does say in the

00:34:22.520 --> 00:34:27.220
manual that there you have to wait at least eight seconds before you can tag again, which I'm

00:34:27.220 --> 00:34:30.400
not sure if that's like an official rule on, on, it's funny.

00:34:30.460 --> 00:34:32.100
Nobody's ever tried that strategy, right?

00:34:32.240 --> 00:34:37.060
Of like tag teaming and just like tag him in, get it, you know, punch him across the face,

00:34:37.160 --> 00:34:38.500
knock him out, tag the next guy.

00:34:38.720 --> 00:34:41.640
And now you're stronger tag, punch him in back and forth.

00:34:41.880 --> 00:34:43.460
Be a fun, be a fun match.

00:34:43.680 --> 00:34:44.820
I'd see that. I'd watch that.

00:34:44.920 --> 00:34:49.380
I'd like to see a tag team, real life tag team wrestling match in which the rules are

00:34:49.380 --> 00:34:52.380
you can't be in the ring for eight seconds without tagging out.

00:34:52.380 --> 00:34:56.180
So like every seven seconds you have to tag out both players.

00:34:56.860 --> 00:34:57.880
Yeah. Oh yeah.

00:34:57.980 --> 00:35:01.360
There's like, there's like a dozen people on each side and they're just wrestling each

00:35:01.360 --> 00:35:09.040
other. If you defeat every other wrestler other than the one you're playing as in the single player

00:35:09.040 --> 00:35:11.820
mode, you will unlock the secret character.

00:35:12.000 --> 00:35:15.060
What is up first off with all wrestling games having a secret character?

00:35:15.060 --> 00:35:20.040
Uh, the secret character in this game is the WCW master who is not real.

00:35:20.280 --> 00:35:21.880
There is no WCW master.

00:35:22.340 --> 00:35:24.160
That, that's stupid. He's seven foot six.

00:35:24.940 --> 00:35:31.400
If there is, if this is a licensed video game and everybody else is real, I don't think that

00:35:31.400 --> 00:35:36.340
the unlockable dude should be a completely made up.

00:35:36.460 --> 00:35:38.480
I don't know. I thought it was going to be master hand.

00:35:39.300 --> 00:35:46.520
Right, right. Uh, I'm trying to think about like who would have been like an awesome secret wrestler for

00:35:46.520 --> 00:35:48.040
the WCW at the time.

00:35:48.460 --> 00:35:54.900
Um, cause if you want somebody who's like seven foot something, uh, the giant, um, who eventually

00:35:54.900 --> 00:35:55.860
became the big show.

00:35:55.920 --> 00:35:57.560
Andrew. What's that?

00:35:57.740 --> 00:35:58.580
Andrew the giant.

00:35:58.940 --> 00:35:59.920
Andre the giant.

00:36:00.320 --> 00:36:01.320
Andrew the giant.

00:36:01.820 --> 00:36:06.500
Uh, Andre the giant is, I mean, maybe he wrestled in the WCW, but I think of him more

00:36:06.500 --> 00:36:07.660
as a WWF wrestler.

00:36:07.660 --> 00:36:12.920
Uh, I was talking about the giant from WCW who became the big show in the WWF.

00:36:13.060 --> 00:36:15.260
Uh, but he didn't join until like 95.

00:36:15.540 --> 00:36:21.080
It looks like, so not a candidate here, but also like, this is a weird crossover between

00:36:21.080 --> 00:36:27.140
like the, this secret character between the giant and like Kane with the mask and stuff.

00:36:27.240 --> 00:36:31.520
It's like, I don't know what they were going for here, but this is, it's just weird.

00:36:31.520 --> 00:36:37.740
It almost feels, uh, like if you dedicated yourself enough to fight all these other WCW

00:36:37.740 --> 00:36:42.160
wrestlers and then just get handed this guy as your reward feels kind of cheap.

00:36:46.600 --> 00:36:51.680
On the sequels and spinoff side, I could talk about WCW sequels, but Sean, you mentioned that

