I also had a game on N64 WCW versus NWO.

00:37:01.460 --> 00:37:03.080
And, um, that was a good game.

00:37:03.200 --> 00:37:04.560
I appreciated that one.

00:37:04.900 --> 00:37:08.900
Um, it was really like, especially for an N64 game though.

00:37:08.900 --> 00:37:15.980
And something that was, I guess like, you know, at the time more for kids and fun and all

00:37:15.980 --> 00:37:17.180
that. It wasn't a lot of fun.

00:37:17.340 --> 00:37:18.820
It felt very technical again.

00:37:19.020 --> 00:37:25.200
It didn't feel like as crazy as the WWF games go in terms of presentational and flair and

00:37:25.200 --> 00:37:30.080
everything. I, I remember thinking as a kid, like, it's weird that the referee's always around and

00:37:30.080 --> 00:37:33.420
he's always watching us and we get counted out if we're outside the ring.

00:37:33.480 --> 00:37:36.360
Like, I just wanted to have like fun, no disqualification matches.

00:37:36.360 --> 00:37:37.640
And that just wasn't even an option.

00:37:37.640 --> 00:37:43.380
That, that was sort of my problem with Nitro is because like, I was playing this PS1 game

00:37:43.380 --> 00:37:50.720
well into the PS2 era and I had played like, uh, uh, the, one of the, you know, the, the

00:37:50.720 --> 00:37:57.080
one, the classic on PS2 that, that, that generation, um, where you get to leave the ring and then

00:37:57.080 --> 00:38:00.700
go backstage and then use whatever props back there that you want.

00:38:01.040 --> 00:38:03.140
On PS2 that would have been like, shut your mouth?

00:38:03.360 --> 00:38:04.360
Something like that.

00:38:04.360 --> 00:38:09.560
And you get the whole like creative, the creative guy was super advanced for the time.

00:38:09.560 --> 00:38:15.000
So when I was like first playing that game and then I was playing Nitro and didn't even

00:38:15.000 --> 00:38:18.320
like, let you leave the, the, the, the arena.

00:38:18.320 --> 00:38:19.640
I was like, what is this?

00:38:19.640 --> 00:38:21.420
I want all my fights to be backstage.

00:38:21.960 --> 00:38:26.340
Um, so yeah, that, that, that left something to be desired.

00:38:26.880 --> 00:38:34.000
Funny story about WWF, uh, or at the time, I guess it was officially now WWE, uh, WWE SmackDown,

00:38:34.000 --> 00:38:35.040
shut your mouth.

00:38:35.420 --> 00:38:36.440
Uh, funny story about that.

00:38:36.600 --> 00:38:41.180
I was at GameStop looking for this game and my dad was nice enough to drive me and we were

00:38:41.180 --> 00:38:45.700
just looking, um, around and he said, he said to me, Mike, what's the name of the game again?

00:38:45.800 --> 00:38:47.060
And I said, shut your mouth.

00:38:47.140 --> 00:38:48.600
And he said, what did you say to me?

00:38:48.660 --> 00:38:50.240
And it was just like a quick funny thing.

00:38:50.380 --> 00:38:52.900
And like, obviously like I told him like, no, that's the name of the game.

00:38:53.060 --> 00:38:56.560
Like, but you know, they definitely like design that kind of situation.

00:38:56.560 --> 00:38:59.700
Right. Now they want to start family fights.

00:38:59.860 --> 00:39:05.120
Yes. Right. No, or just like say that, you know, you don't want to call it WWE SmackDown, shut your mouth.

00:39:05.220 --> 00:39:08.720
Right. Like you wanted to, they wanted it shorthand, shut your mouth as the name of the game.

00:39:09.040 --> 00:39:13.340
What's funny is, is that it would continue to follow that line of thinking for all the

00:39:13.340 --> 00:39:15.240
other SmackDown games across that era.

00:39:15.440 --> 00:39:18.460
So they even had, uh, just bring it as a game.

00:39:18.460 --> 00:39:20.960
And maybe that would have been funnier if I told my dad, like, just bring it.

00:39:21.500 --> 00:39:23.260
Yeah. Like you're challenging them to a fight.

00:39:23.540 --> 00:39:25.760
I prefer shut your mouth. And then he'll get the answer to your question.

00:39:25.760 --> 00:39:27.420
Not even challenge them to a fight, Joe.

00:39:27.540 --> 00:39:29.560
I'm thinking like, don't ask me the name of the game.

00:39:29.760 --> 00:39:30.600
Just bring it to me.

00:39:32.220 --> 00:39:34.900
You know, this used to happen to me with Nickelodeon's figure it out.

00:39:35.140 --> 00:39:36.220
My mom would be like, what are you watching?

00:39:36.340 --> 00:39:37.400
And I'd be like, figure it out.

00:39:37.960 --> 00:39:39.980
Ooh. Very nice.

00:39:40.100 --> 00:39:40.980
Yeah. Don't give me that lip.

00:39:41.520 --> 00:39:45.820
Uh, on the real sequels and spinoff side though, I just want to say that, uh, obviously,

00:39:46.120 --> 00:39:51.500
uh, this game before it became WCW licensed had like a Famicom version first.

00:39:51.500 --> 00:39:58.780
And that was Superstar Pro Wrestling, which, uh, featured wrestlers from Japan's AJPW and

00:39:59.420 --> 00:40:04.800
NJPW promotions, uh, which are, you know, a big deal, uh, in the wrestling world, but

00:40:04.800 --> 00:40:05.820
also obviously in Japan.

00:40:05.820 --> 00:40:10.680
And so, uh, that game also featured, you know, different licensed characters.

00:40:10.880 --> 00:40:19.700
So that's kind of cool. I guess it's also just interesting that, um, you couldn't just do like a, like a, a color

00:40:19.700 --> 00:40:26.060
swap. You had to, they had to, when you're localizing this game, they had to like reanimate everything

00:40:26.060 --> 00:40:27.860
because there's like different moves too.

00:40:28.020 --> 00:40:31.780
Right. And, and just, yeah, that the actual wrestlers look different too.

00:40:31.920 --> 00:40:35.180
Like you can't just say like, yeah, Ric Flair today, he's just going to look like this

00:40:35.180 --> 00:40:39.780
Japanese guy. Although I think there was like.

00:40:41.320 --> 00:40:44.300
One character was in both of them or something like that.

00:40:44.760 --> 00:40:50.540
Road Warrior Hawk, um, is in both versions of the game.

00:40:50.540 --> 00:40:51.900
It seems like that's kind of cool.

00:40:52.500 --> 00:40:56.360
Wow. Less, less work for the, for the North America team.

00:40:57.580 --> 00:41:02.820
And Sean, since I'm looking here, it says WCW master is based on Andre the giant, but

