everything. Like technically in a, you know, in later games that would include both of them, they would

00:43:30.380 --> 00:43:34.420
be different kinds of wrestlers, not just because their move sets are different, but just because

00:43:34.420 --> 00:43:37.140
there are more than one type of wrestler.

00:43:37.340 --> 00:43:42.480
There isn't just this idea that, uh, everybody punches and everybody kicks.

00:43:42.480 --> 00:43:43.640
Cause it doesn't work like that.

00:43:43.760 --> 00:43:45.840
Uh, if it did wrestling would be fairly boring.

00:43:46.120 --> 00:43:51.480
So, uh, this still doesn't quite put wrestling games on the NES over the edge.

00:43:51.620 --> 00:43:55.140
And so Mike three 16 says, I just whooped this game's ass.

00:43:55.340 --> 00:43:57.880
Sean. Yeah.

